Ladybird’s archive reader refuses entries whose names leave the
destination, symbolic links, case-only duplicates, and archives past
its size and count limits, and it checks every entry’s CRC. Gecko reads
an .xpi with its nsIZipReader in XPIInstall.sys.mjs, and Chromium’s
zip reader (third_party/zlib/google/zip_reader.cc) likewise refuses a
“..” part in an entry’s path.
